Author: Antonio De Leon [aut, cre],
    Raquel Prado [aut],
    Bruno Sanso [aut]
Maintainer: Antonio De Leon <jaguir26@ucsc.edu>
Description: Research implementation of mean-preserving interval (MPI) and
    mean-tilted interval (MTI) losses, generalized-Bayesian root regression,
    scan-calibrated and split exact-spacing tolerance actions, and Bayesian
    nonparametric shortest-interval uncertainty. The normal-exponential
    construction augments an exponentiated interval loss and is not a response
    likelihood. Deterministic Cornish-Fisher and empirical pilots provide fixed
    mean-tilt initialization anchors without sampling the tilt. Fixed-target
    ECM computes deterministic generalized-posterior modes from exact inverse
    latent-scale moments while remaining separate from posterior sampling.
    Direct Dirichlet-process and truncated Gaussian DPM response-distribution
    engines provide the authoritative Bayesian UQ layer for shortest-interval
    content and hybrid Bayesian-scan tolerance actions.
